ver; existing Stores acquire the released lock after a writer crash and read old trust beside the replaced configuration. Port the reviewer probes RED first on the current source: TestReviewerCrashBetweenConfigAndGeneration (child exit 77 at the real config rename; surviving LoadCoherent must refuse or converge, never admit old generation 3) and TestReviewerRollbackCrashSurvivingReader (real rollbackV4 child exit 77 at the replacement seam; surviving LoadCoherent must not admit old generation 4); keep TestReviewerCrashReopenConverges green. Repair the production mechanism: make the pending joint-commit marker a general admission barrier so every read, admission and transaction entry point (WithSharedSnapshot/readSnapshotLocked, readCommitted, authorization boundaries, mutation transactions) recovers or refuses unresolved intent under the authorization lock before exposing a snapshot or running a boundary. Preserve stale-request refusal — never silently refresh a stale request to the recovered generation. Cover surviving and reopened processes, apply and rollback, and marker cleanup/error ordering with real child-process tests. Fix TestApplyV4CrashConvergesGeneration so it asserts convergence with fatal expectations instead of returning silently on Load/Configuration/Open/ReadSnapshot errors; distinguish a tested refusal from a proven recovery. This was already flagged by parent nudge fd9186 — repair the assertions and evidence, do not restate the claim.\n4|\n5|F2 (P1, row 12): concurrent first-open replaces a held lock inode. Unix openLock does Lstat-absent, CreateTemp, replacing Rename; lockInitMu protects only one process. Port TestReviewerCrossProcessLockInitialization RED first (child paused after the absence observation, parent creates and holds the lock, child replaces it and returns while held: returnedWhileHeld=true, sameInode=false on Darwin). Implement atomic, non-replacing lock initialization shared by all processes (for example O_CREAT|O_EXCL creation or