{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c449","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0aa44-08d9-7882-b782-d653915eefd3"},"sequence":127,"recorded_at":1780531400000249,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"bc8ec94b-72dd-41ff-812d-ceee7d051537","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"bc8ec94b-72dd-41ff-812d-ceee7d051537","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"bc8ec94b-72dd-41ff-812d-ceee7d051537"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0aa44-48dc-76c2-a2f5-f848efdfcc1c"},"task_id":"01a0aa44-48dc-76c2-a2f5-f848efdfcc1c","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0aa44-48dc-76c2-a2f5-f848efdfcc1c","chunk":"Read text file `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/resources/TASK-260909-2ez769/TASK-260909-2ez769_review-verdict-rev4.md`.\n1|# Revision 4 review: changes requested\n2|\n3|TASK-260909-2ez769 / CR-TASK-260909-2ez769-4 revision 4.\n4|Base: a89328ca85a613abde39660f4be749a8fcf57903.\n5|Candidate tree: 2c8909c9c7425bb3a90c00b8db3762f43b4dbf39.\n6|Review against an immutable archive; no managed-worktree product edits, commits, integration or landing.\n7|\n8|## Blocking findings\n9|\n10|### F1 — P1: surviving processes accept an interrupted config/trust pair\n11|\n12|`internal/hosttrust/transact.go`, `WithSharedSnapshot`/`readSnapshotLocked`, and\n13|`internal/hosttrust/authorize.go`, `readCommitted`, never inspect the pending\n14|joint-commit marker. Recovery happens only in `Open` (or explicit `Recover`).\n15|The exclusive OS lock disappears when the writer crashes, but other processes\n16|with already-open Stores remain alive and can acquire it and read old trust\n17|alongside the replaced configuration. Locking alone does not make that pair a\n18|committed pair. The same omission reaches authorization and ordinary trust\n19|transactions; the marker is not a general admission barrier.\n20|\n21|Executed real child-process probes against the candidate:\n22|\n23|- `TestReviewerCrashBetweenConfigAndGeneration`: production `applyV4` exits 77\n24|  after the real config rename; surviving parent's production `LoadCoherent`\n25|  succeeds with the replaced configuration and generation 3 (the old value).\n26|  Parent test FAIL, go test exit 1.\n27|- `TestReviewerRollbackCrashSurvivingReader`: first performs real `ApplyV4`, then\n28|  production `rollbackV4` child exits 77 at the replacement seam; surviving\n29|  `LoadCoherent` succeeds with generation 4 (the old value). FAIL, exit 1.\n30|- `TestReviewerCrashReopenConverges`: a fresh `Open` after the apply crash does\n31|  converge and passes with fatal assertions on read/open errors. This repair\n32|  works for new openers, but does not cover surviving processes.\n33|\n34|Repair all read/admission/transaction entry points under the authorization lock\n35|so unresolved intent is recovered or refused before exposing a snapshot or\n36|running a boundary. Cover both apply and rollback, surviving processes as well\n37|as reopen, and marker cleanup/error ordering. Do not silently refresh a stale\n38|request to the recovered generation. Section 11.10.3 requires coherent committed\n39|reads across processes, not just after reopening a Store.\n40|\n41|The shipped `TestApplyV4CrashConvergesGeneration` still returns success early on\n42|Load, Configuration, Open and ReadSnapshot errors (migration_v4_apply_test.go,\n43|roughly lines 419–436). Those branches cannot prove successful convergence.\n44|Replace them with explicit expectations, distinguishing a tested refusal from\n45|successful recovery. No shipped rollback child-crash test was found.\n46|\n47|### F2 — P1: concurrent first-open replaces a held authorization lock\n48|\n49|`internal/hosttrust/lock_unix.go`, `openLock`, uses Lstat-absent followed by\n50|CreateTemp and replacing Rename. `lockInitMu` serializes only goroutines in one\n51|process. Two processes can both observe absence; the delayed process renames\n52|its staged lock over the first process's already-held lock. Subsequent locks\n53|then attach to a different inode and no longer serialize.\n54|\n55|`TestReviewerCrossProcessLockInitialization` deterministically pauses a real\n56|child's production `openStore` after its absent-lock Lstat. Parent `Open` creates\n57|the lock, initializes trust and holds an exclusive acquisition. Releasing the\n58|child allows its `Open` to finish while the parent still holds the old lock.\n59|The test verifies both facts: `returnedWhileHeld=true sameInode=false`.\n60|FAIL, exit 1 on Darwin/arm64. Only the filesystem observation is synchronized;\n61|creation, rename, Open and locking are production code against OS files.\n62|\n63|Use atomic non-replacing lock initialization shared by all processes; never\n64|replace a live lock inode. Exercise concurrent first-open and existing-lock\n65|contention through production entry points. Inspect the analogous Windows\n66|initialization path too. Do not infer a native Windows failure from this Darwin\n67|execution.\n68|\n69|### F3 — P2: remaining acceptance/evidence claims exceed their reach\n70|\n71|- Native Windows DACL read/install code now exists; CR3's owner-SID-only\n72|  implementation criticism is no longer accurate. However `TestOwnerOnlyGrants`\n73|  is a pure evaluator and cross-build/vet do not execute native owner-only,\n74|  other-principal or reparse acceptance/refusal. There are no native Windows\n75|  tests in the candidate. Row 15 is not production-driven. No observed leak is\n76|  claimed. Add the native tests and actual platform evidence required by scope;\n77|  accurately retain unavailable runtime evidence as unverified.\n78|- The config writer stages backups using Chmod only; the producer expressly\n79|  leaves Windows backup DACLs to profile inheritance. The direct 11.10.2\n80|  owner-only clause governs credential custody, so I do not assert every plain\n81|  configuration backup is a leaked private key. Still, inherited profile ACLs\n82|  are not evidence of owner-only access. Classify the actual backup contents\n83|  and applicable contract rather than claiming this bound proves custody.\n84|- `MatchExcludedFromReplication` and `ExcludedConfigDirName` still have only\n85|  test callers. The outcome supplies a generic future-consumer instruction,\n86|  but no named owning downstream task or corresponding attached API/test\n87|  handoff. Implemented matcher tests are useful and public enrollment remains\n88|  separate; they do not establish exclusion through replication/snapshot/clone/\n89|  Session Directory/diagnostic consumers. Persist the precise ownership handoff\n90|  for unavailable consumers, as CR3 F5 permits, and count row 21 honestly.\n91|- Config label-precision mutation accounting was corrected. Retain that fix.\n92|  Three newly affected hosttrust narrowing plants fail the expected named tests,\n93|  and the applied harmless control survives. These do not cover F1/F2.\n94|\n95|## Independent AC accounting\n96|\n97|**19 of 21 functional AC rows driven**, of which 16 have bounded passing\n98|candidate evidence and 3 have failing reviewer counterexamples. Rows 15 and 21\n99|are not driven at the required native/consumer entry points. This is the same\n100|21-row functional decomposition used in CR3, not a claim of every normative\n101|clause or every gate covered. A driven row can fail.\n102|\n103|| # | Row | Production call / named test | Result |\n104||---|---|---|---|\n105||1|Closed Config4|Decode / TestDecodeConfiguration4Refusals|Pass|\n106||2|Historical compatibility, explicit migration|Migrate / TestMigrateRefusesV4Target, TestMigrateRefusesV4Downgrade|Pass|\n107||3|Closed trust document|DecodeTrust / TestDecodeTrustRefusals|Pass|\n108||4|Missing/corrupt trust|ReadSnapshot / TestReadSnapshotMissingStore, TestCorruptTrustRefusedNeverEmpty|Pass, ordinary paths|\n109||5|Fresh issuance|IssueCredential / TestIssueCredentialProfile|Pass|\n110||6|Profile/time bounds|VerifyProfile / TestVerifyProfileRefusals, TestVerifyProfileRefusesJustPastExpiry|Pass|\n111||7|Explicit enrollment|Store.Enroll / TestEnrollRefusals|Pass; OOB verification remains operator act|\n112||8|Unique mapping|DecodeTrust / TestDecodeTrustRefusals duplicate-root/key cases|Pass|\n113||9|Rotation/retirement|Rotate, MarkRetiring / TestRotateBoundedWindow, TestMarkRetiringCapsAtLeafExpiry|Pass|\n114||10|Revocation tombstones|Revoke, Enroll / TestRevokeTombstone, TestRevokedLeafNeverReenrolls|Pass, serial paths|\n115||11|Stale mutation refusal|WithMutationAuthorization / TestReviewerStaleMutation|Pass, repaired|\n116||12|Shared authorization serialization|Open/openLock / TestReviewerCrossProcessLockInitialization; WithMutationAuthorization/Revoke / TestReviewerRevocationDuringBoundary and TestReviewerSeparateStoreRevocationDuringBoundary|FAIL first-open; existing same/separate-Store contention passes|\n117||13|Coherent config/trust readers|LoadCoherent / TestReviewerCrashBetweenConfigAndGeneration, TestReviewerRollbackCrashSurvivingReader|FAIL surviving readers|\n118||14|Unix custody|Open, ValidateCustody / TestCustodyRefusals, TestValidateCustodyBindsDirectory|Pass on Darwin|\n119||15|Windows equivalent ACLs|verifyOwner/installOwnerOnlyACL; only TestOwnerOnlyGrants model test|Not native-driven|\n120||16|Complete peers/local credential|PreviewV4 / TestPreviewV4PeerEnrollment, TestPreviewV4CredentialGates|Pass|\n121||17|Exact preview/confirmation|ApplyV4 / TestApplyV4PreviewMismatch, TestApplyV4ConfirmRequiredWithDrops|Pass|\n122||18|Current source/generation apply|ApplyV4 / TestApplyV4StaleSource, TestApplyV4StaleGeneration|Pass; in-lock helper tests additionally present|\n123||19|Crash-durable pair/recovery|applyV4, rollbackV4, LoadCoherent / reviewer crash tests above|FAIL surviving readers; fresh apply reopen passes|\n124||20|Explicit rollback|RollbackV4 / TestRollbackV4, TestRollbackV4BackupGates|Pass ordinary/error paths; crash bound in row19|\n125||21|Secret exclusion across consumers|MatchExcludedFromReplication/ExcludedConfigDirName / helper tests only|Not consumer-driven; precise ownership handoff incomplete|\n126|\n127|RPC handshake, actual dispatch, watchdog and operator distribution boundaries\n128|remain unchanged. No transport work is requested from this leaf. Power-loss\n129|persistence remains distinct from the executed process-crash tests.\n130|\n131|## Verification, preservation and logs\n132|\n133|- Candidate patch SHA256 matches 73975946c2f994f11b3434e7923c689e1eefe9439e94d5d3d0a2cc53fa9bbf28.\n134|  Base signature verifies for oparin@me.com and contains adoption trunk 8cf4aaa.\n135|- RPC backup 15/15 and parked files 11/11 match stored hashes. None of the 49\n136|  candidate paths overlaps the RPC manifest. Preservation outcome is still on\n137|  TASK-260830-z1yxg9. Existing checkpointed SSH/peer bytes are preserved.\n138|- Independently reran immutable hosttrust/config/peeridentity package tests\n139|  `-count=1 -cover`: exit 0, coverage 77.8% / 93.1% / 97.5%.\n140|- Reviewer authorization probes: exit 0, all three named tests PASS. Crash\n141|  probe group: exit 1, two named FAIL and fresh-reopen PASS. Cross-process lock\n142|  initialization: exit 1. Child exit 77 is asserted, not inferred.\n143|- Re-executed neutral, stale-mutation-refresh, joint-marker-stale, recover-diverged\n144|  overlays: neutral exit 0, three plants exit 1 with their expected named\n145|  failures; harness exit 0. Probe-only files were removed from discovery first.\n146|- Producer source manifests match immutable candidate (29 hosttrust, 8 config\n147|  files); retained producer mutation results report 18 hosttrust semantic kills\n148|  plus neutral and 4 config semantic kills plus 1 label kill and neutral.\n149|- Reused rev4 attached build/vet/full-suite/publication evidence instead of\n150|  rerunning unrelated suites. Its bounded validation log shows board issues\n151|  despite an exit-0 board command; that is not proof of a clean board. These\n152|  checks cannot override reproduced failures. No native Windows execution.\n153|- Initial setup mistakes are not evidence: first probe command selected no\n154|  tests in the live tree; first stale probe used an already-issued host and\n155|  failed fixture setup. Both were corrected and superseded by the recorded\n156|  immutable candidate runs. No product files were edited by either attempt.\n157|- Review scratch: .temp/TASK-260909-2ez769/review4. Attached evidence ZIP contains\n158|  probe source, reproducible commands, source/provenance checks, logs and mutant\n159|  results. Required skills loaded; Go skill resolved through main checkout's\n160|  Curator adapter because this worktree lacks adapters. No tools installed.\n161|\n162|## Verdict and routing\n163|\n164|Changes requested. Route TASK-260909-2ez769 to to-dev; do not accept revision 4.\n165|This is ordinary implementable rework, not Stop-The-Line. Preserve the managed\n166|base, RPC packet and all accepted work. Do not supply commit_ack or integrate.","final_result":true}}}
