{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000de09","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0aa44-08d9-7882-b782-d653915eefd3"},"sequence":3423,"recorded_at":1780531400006841,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"bc8ec94b-72dd-41ff-812d-ceee7d051537","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"bc8ec94b-72dd-41ff-812d-ceee7d051537","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"bc8ec94b-72dd-41ff-812d-ceee7d051537"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0aa60-b78c-7b42-a6d5-73de92b99766"},"task_id":"01a0aa60-b78c-7b42-a6d5-73de92b99766","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0aa60-b78c-7b42-a6d5-73de92b99766","chunk":"{\n  \"chunk_id\": \"exec-71-1\",\n  \"command\": \"grep -rn \\\"cataloggen\\\" --include=\\\"*.md\\\" --include=\\\"*.yml\\\" --include=\\\"*.yaml\\\" --include=\\\"Makefile\\\" --include=\\\"*.mk\\\" --include=\\\"*.sh\\\" . 2>/dev/null | grep -v \\\".temp/\\\" | grep -v node_modules | head -8; ls .github/workflows/ 2>/dev/null\",\n  \"description\": \"Find cataloggen invocation pattern\",\n  \"exit_code\": 0,\n  \"terminal_status\": \"completed\",\n  \"scan_scope_hint\": \"[hint] unscoped recursive scan over the workspace root — scope the next search to the subtree the task names or use the bounded search tool; if this scan backgrounded, harvest or terminate it before ending the turn.\",\n  \"output\": \"./LOGBOOK.md:10:- COMBINE: worktree restored to candidate snapshot by tool; 30 enumerated incoming paths restored from HEAD (8 adoption files incl. SPEC.v0.6.0.md, v0.6.0.lock.json, ownership.v0.6.0.json, task-board.config.json v0.6.0 cataloggen command); 6 tracked candidate files untouched by adoption kept; LOGBOOK re-merged (HEAD + 2 prior credential entries). Candidate bytes verified 40/40 match pre-refresh fingerprint.\\n./LOGBOOK.md:42:- RECOVERY: prior CR1 failed command 21 because task-board.config.json still passed v0.5.0 inputs to the strict v0.6.0 generator. Changed only that command in candidate and authorized control root; control-root pre-existing config diff was empty and both complete config files now match. TestConfiguredCRCatalogGateConsumesAdoptedAuthority drives the configured command through cataloggen.run and refuses stale authority. No model, signing, required gate or hosted-trigger policy changed.\\n./LOGBOOK.md:79:- CARRIED (pre-existing, fixed here): `//go:generate` → `// go:generate` disarmed the generator while the token survived and the freshness diff stayed clean (reproduced: old step exits 0 on the rewrite). Fix: anchored `grep -c '^//go:generate'` pin in the freshness step + committed `TestGenerateDirectiveStaysRecognizedForm`; the rewrite now fails the guard (exit 1) and the pin while catalog/cataloggen stay otherwise green (battery G-directive-space, behavioral suite executed).\\n./LOGBOOK.md:631:- ROOT CAUSE: **a clause was claimed against a topically related section instead of against the actor its MUST binds.** Ownership clause `15.1#6` at SPEC.md:11047 was discharged by `LocalFromUntrusted`. That line's only RFC 2119 sentence is \\\"The plugin MUST NOT masquerade a different-major object as v2\\\" - it binds the **provider plugin**, a child process this repository does not build; its only binaries are `cataloggen` and `tracecheck`. The host half of the same table row, which `LocalFromUntrusted` does implement, carries no RFC 2119 keyword at all, so it is not what the clause scanner measured.\\n./LOGBOOK.md:710:- EVIDENCE: `go run ./internal/traceability/cmd/tracecheck -section 15.2` exited **0**. §15.2 is the nineteen-row normative exit-code registry (SPEC.md:11073-11095) and nothing in the tree implements it — the only `os.Exit` calls are the `exit(1)` paths of `cataloggen` and `tracecheck`. Same for `-section 7.3`, the closed Provider Manifest, whose sole trace is a catalog row naming its URN. Both were bound to `internal/catalog/catalog.go:ForRelease`, an unrelated symbol.\\n./LOGBOOK.md:800:- STATUS: `internal/canonicaljson` 97.2% before and after, verified against a `git archive HEAD` baseline. gofmt, `go build ./...`, both cross-compile targets, `go vet ./...`, `go test ./... -count=1`, `-cover -count=1`, `-race -count=1`, tracecheck, `cataloggen -check` and all five fuzz gates at 100x exit 0.\\n./LOGBOOK.md:812:- STATUS: `internal/localstore` unchanged at 86.6%, 90 top-level tests and 130 subtests — this round added assertions to existing cases, not new cases. gofmt, `go build ./...`, `go vet ./...`, `go test ./... -count=1`, `-race -count=1`, `-cover -count=1`, both cross-compile targets, global tracecheck, `cataloggen -check` and `git diff --check` all exit 0.\\n./LOGBOOK.md:840:- STATUS: BUG-260902-3v8ck5 on `task-board/story/STORY-260902-2rngvr`, uncommitted candidate at checkpoint `f20aeec`; canonicaljson 97.2% and every other package unchanged against a detached-worktree baseline at the same commit; `go build ./...`, `go vet ./...`, `gofmt -l internal/`, `go test ./... -cover -count=1`, global tracecheck, `go generate ./internal/catalog`, `cataloggen -check` and all five seeded fuzz targets exit 0; handed off to review.\\nci.yml\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 3732,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 933,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}","final_result":true}}}
