{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000e7c7","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0aa44-08d9-7882-b782-d653915eefd3"},"sequence":4670,"recorded_at":1780531400009335,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"bc8ec94b-72dd-41ff-812d-ceee7d051537","payload_type":"run.terminal.completed","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"run_terminal","command_id":"bc8ec94b-72dd-41ff-812d-ceee7d051537","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"bc8ec94b-72dd-41ff-812d-ceee7d051537"},"terminal":"completed","text":"Ready for review — handed off to review.\n\nTASK-260909-2ez769 rework rev5 is complete. All three CR4 findings were repaired with production mechanisms, verified RED-first with the exact reviewer probes (exit 1 each), and handed off with the candidate left uncommitted in the Story worktree.\n\nWhat changed:\n- **F1 — surviving crash readers**: the pending joint-commit marker is now a general admission barrier. Every read, admission, and transaction entry point converges pending intent (or refuses) under the authorization lock before exposing a snapshot — shared readers upgrade to exclusive only when a marker is present. Stale bindings compare against the recovered generation and refuse; nothing is silently refreshed. Real child-process crash tests (exit 77) cover surviving and reopened readers across apply and rollback, plus marker cleanup and intervened-refusal ordering. The silently-returning crash test now uses fatal assertions.\n- **F2 — cross-process lock init**: lock creation is atomic and non-replacing (O_CREAT|O_EXCL / CREATE_NEW) on both unix and Windows; race losers open the existing inode instead of splitting the lock. A deterministic first-open contention test pins the fix; the replacing-rename mutant reproduces the exact reviewer failure shape.\n- **F3 — evidence reach**: native Windows custody tests written (vet + test-compile pass; runtime honestly unverified), config backups classified by contents and contract with a pinning test, and the row-21 downstream handoff persisted as a board outcome with notes on all 7 owned tasks — diagnostics explicitly flagged as unowned.\n\nEvidence: 19 of 21 AC rows driven through production entry points (rows 15 and 21 bounded, not passed); mutation batteries rerun on exact final source (hosttrust 25 narrowing + 1 paired call-site killed with neutral surviving; config 4 semantic + 1 label killed with neutral passing; every exit from real command status); full local CI replicated green including race, coverage, tracecheck, catalog freshness, cigate gates, 13 fuzz smokes, and fixtures. Preservation re-verified: RPC backup 15/15, parked delta 11/11, no RPC/SSH/peer bytes in the candidate.","reason":null}}
